menu "Shahbaz production composition"

config SHAHBAZ_ACTUATORS_ENABLE
    bool "Enable physical PWM actuator outputs"
    default n
    help
        Keep disabled for sensor-only bench builds. When enabled, the
        production composition still fails closed unless the exact-board
        actuator GPIO review evidence is configured, the pins validate as
        available-with-review GPIOs, and runtime memory validation passes.
        The board exposes four motor PWM outputs and two optional servo PWM
        outputs only after that gate succeeds.

config SHAHBAZ_ALLOW_LEGACY_INDIVIDUAL_MOTOR_COMMANDS
    bool "Allow legacy single-motor Protocol v2 commands (unsafe compatibility)"
    default n
    depends on SHAHBAZ_ACTUATORS_ENABLE
    help
        Keep disabled for every production and flight profile. When enabled,
        the dispatcher accepts legacy MotorCommand and motor-targeted generic
        ActuatorCommand messages that can change one rotor independently. This
        option exists only for deliberate migration/bench compatibility; the
        coherent MotorFrameCommand remains the required flight-control path.

endmenu
